<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.guardian.bedrockwatch.plist

  The Bedrock watcher: something that notices when the iPad finally tries to
  join the world.

  WHY THIS EXISTS

  The crossplay question has never been answered because the iPad has never
  joined. Every attempt so far has been a person opening Minecraft on
  Cyber-Portal and watching. That works right up until the watching has to
  outlive a session — which is exactly what happened: the watcher was a
  background task that died every hour and had to be re-armed.

  A watcher whose lifetime is shorter than the thing it waits for is not a
  watcher. So it is a job.

  WHAT IT WATCHES FOR

  Anything Bedrock-shaped in the server log: Geyser's own accept and refuse
  lines, Floodgate's, any player join, any disconnect. The refusals are the
  interesting ones — they say WHY a client was turned away, which is the
  difference between "the version is too new" and "the transport is wrong".

  It also writes a heartbeat every thirty seconds. A watcher that reports
  "nothing happened" has to be able to report "I am still watching" with the
  same confidence, because a dead pipeline and a quiet server look
  identical otherwise.

  It never touches the world. It only reads the log.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.guardian.bedrockwatch</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
      <string>/bin/bash</string>
      <string>/Users/resonant_jones/Keep/MineCraft_Companion/minecraft-ai-companion/scripts/runBedrockWatch.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/resonant_jones/Keep/MineCraft_Companion/minecraft-ai-companion</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- If the watcher dies, bring it back. A dead watcher is a visible
         failure, unlike a dead pilot. -->
    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <true/>

    <key>LimitLoadToSessionType</key>
    <array>
      <string>Aqua</string>
    </array>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/resonant_jones/Keep/MineCraft_Companion/minecraft-ai-companion/.local/logs/bedrockwatch.out</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/resonant_jones/Keep/MineCraft_Companion/minecraft-ai-companion/.local/logs/bedrockwatch.err</string>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
  </dict>
</plist>
